# Session 1: Phase 0 (Skeleton Implementation) — Go + Gin

## Purpose
Execute Session 1 to create a fully functional API skeleton where all endpoints return mock data
matching the OpenAPI specification. This establishes project structure, enables E2E test writing, and
validates API contracts before any real business logic exists.

## CRITICAL: This Session Stops After Skeleton - No Endpoint Implementation

DO NOT:
- Implement real business logic
- Create database migrations
- Create GORM models beyond what's needed for mock handler DTOs
- Create repositories or services
- Proceed to Session 2 automatically

ONLY:
- Create project structure
- Implement mock handlers
- Set up Docker Compose
- Configure environment
- Create test scaffolding

Session 2 (first real endpoint implementation) is a SEPARATE session that requires explicit user command.

## Session Prerequisites
- OpenAPI specification complete and validated
- Plan folder structure created with session plans
- Session 1 plan reviewed (`plan/sessions/session-1-phase-0.md`)
- Go toolchain and golangci-lint installed

