### 5. Mock Handler Implementation

For each endpoint in the OpenAPI spec, create a mock handler.

**Pattern for POST endpoints:**
```go
// CreatePost handles POST /api/posts — MOCK IMPLEMENTATION (Phase 0).
func CreatePost(c *gin.Context) {
    var req CreatePostRequest
    if err := c.ShouldBindJSON(&req); err != nil {
        c.JSON(http.StatusBadRequest, gin.H{"error": err.Error()})
        return
    }

    c.JSON(http.StatusCreated, PostResponse{
        PostID:    "mock-123",
        Title:     req.Title,
        Content:   req.Content,
        AuthorID:  "mock-author-123",
        CreatedAt: "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z",
    })
}
```

**Pattern for GET (single resource) endpoints:**
```go
// GetPost handles GET /api/posts/:id — MOCK IMPLEMENTATION (Phase 0).
func GetPost(c *gin.Context) {
    postID := c.Param("id")

    c.JSON(http.StatusOK, PostResponse{
        PostID:    postID,
        Title:     "Mock Post Title",
        Content:   "Mock post content here",
        AuthorID:  "mock-author-123",
        CreatedAt: "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z",
    })
}
```

**Pattern for GET (list) endpoints:**
```go
// ListPosts handles GET /api/posts — MOCK IMPLEMENTATION (Phase 0).
func ListPosts(c *gin.Context) {
    c.JSON(http.StatusOK, gin.H{
        "posts": []PostResponse{
            {PostID: "mock-123", Title: "Mock Post 1", AuthorID: "mock-author-123", CreatedAt: "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z"},
            {PostID: "mock-124", Title: "Mock Post 2", AuthorID: "mock-author-123", CreatedAt: "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z"},
        },
        "totalCount": 2,
    })
}
```

### 6. Request/Response DTO Structs
Create Go structs matching the OpenAPI schemas, in `internal/model/`.

Go idiom: use flat, separate structs per operation — there is no Pydantic-style inheritance chain.

```go
// internal/model/post.go

// CreatePostRequest is the API request body for creating a post.
type CreatePostRequest struct {
    Title    string `json:"title" binding:"required,min=1,max=200"`
    Content  string `json:"content" binding:"required,min=1"`
    AuthorID string `json:"authorId" binding:"required"`
}

// PostResponse is the API response body representing a post.
type PostResponse struct {
    PostID    string `json:"postId"`
    Title     string `json:"title"`
    Content   string `json:"content"`
    AuthorID  string `json:"authorId"`
    CreatedAt string `json:"createdAt"`
}
```

### 7. Router Registration
Wire mock handlers into the router in `cmd/server/main.go` or a dedicated `internal/handler/routes.go`:

```go
func RegisterRoutes(r *gin.Engine) {
    r.GET("/health", HealthCheck)

    api := r.Group("/api")
    {
        posts := api.Group("/posts")
        {
            posts.POST("", CreatePost)
            posts.GET("/:id", GetPost)
            posts.GET("", ListPosts)
        }
    }
}
```

### 8. Testing Setup
Create test scaffolding (colocated `_test.go` files are idiomatic Go):
```
internal/handler/
├── health.go
├── health_test.go
├── posts.go
└── posts_test.go
```

Set `gin.SetMode(gin.TestMode)` in test setup to suppress debug output.

