go test ./internal/handler/... -v
```

## Mock Data Guidelines

### Consistency
Use consistent mock IDs across related endpoints:
- Post ID: `"mock-123"`
- Author ID: `"mock-author-123"`
- Comment ID: `"mock-comment-456"`

### Realistic Structure
Mock responses should match production structure:
- Include all required fields
- Use proper JSON types
- Include timestamps in RFC3339/ISO format
- Return appropriate HTTP status codes (`201` for creation, `200` for reads, `204` for deletes)

### Error Cases
Implement mock error responses:
```go
func GetPost(c *gin.Context) {
    postID := c.Param("id")
    if postID == "error" {
        c.JSON(http.StatusNotFound, gin.H{"error": "post not found"})
        return
    }
    // ... mock success response
}
```

